"""Adroit pen reorientation: a library of open-loop joint trajectories, picked per target, with start-pose planning.

Control law
-----------
* Library: each entry is a joint-space trajectory given by 5 knots (control steps KN = 0, 30, 60, 100, 140) of the
  24 normalised servo set points, linearly interpolated and held after the last knot.  The entries were found offline
  by derivative-free cross-entropy search in the simulator (no learning, nothing optimised at run time); most were
  scored jointly on the nominal, heavy and slippery plants and on random jittered pen starts, so that they hold the pen
  at the same final axis on all of them.  Stored with every entry: the final pen axis it produces on the nominal,
  heavy, slippery, weak and shaken plants (LIB_AX) and the finite-difference sensitivity J (3 x 6) of that final axis
  to constant set-point offsets [rad] of the six trim joints WRJ1, WRJ0, THJ4, THJ3, THJ1, LFJ4 (LIB_J).
* Selection (step 0): every entry is scored by its expected success for the observed target axis t, the mean over the
  stored plants of sigmoid((cos(u, t) - SEL_COS) / SEL_TEMP) for its final axes u (SEL_COS sets the cosine margin
  asked for, SEL_TEMP how sharply it is asked); the best entry is played back.  SEL_TRIM in [0, 1] lets the score
  count on the trim feedback below to close part of the gap (0 = not at all).
* Start-pose planning: when the joint readings at step 0 are noise-free but the pen does not start at the package's
  pose (a jittered start), the jitter (x, y offset and turn about the vertical) is read off the observation, the
  PLAN_N best-scored entries are rolled out on a private copy of the nominal plant (hl_control's own model) from that
  start, and the one whose simulated final axis stays closest to the target is played back (about 30 ms per entry,
  once per episode).
* Trim feedback (optional, off by default: FB_GAIN = 0 did best in tests): from step FB_START the error t - u between
  target and low-passed (FB_ALPHA) measured axis is mapped through the damped (FB_DAMP) pseudo-inverse of J, or with
  FB_WRIST = 1 through the exact kinematic map of hand rotations about -z (WRJ1) and +x (WRJ0), and integrated with
  gain FB_GAIN into the trim offsets, each bounded by TRIM_MAX [rad].

Reach: targets tilted toward the thumb side (+x) are reached and held reliably; near-vertical targets and targets
tilted toward -x are beyond the motions in the library.
"""
